.TH RUNNER 1 "2026-07-30" "irix-actions-runner 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runner \- GitHub Actions self-hosted runner for SGI IRIX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runner configure
.B \-\-url
.I URL
.B \-\-token
.I TOKEN
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B runner run
.RI [ \-\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RI [ \-\-verbose | \-\-trace ]
.br
.B runner serve
.RI [ \-\-count
.I N
.B \-\-name\-prefix
.IR P ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B runner execjob
.B \-\-message
.I FILE
.B \-\-name
.I NAME
.B \-\-work
.I DIR
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B runner remove
.B \-\-token
.I TOKEN
.RI [ \-\-count
.I N
.B \-\-name\-prefix
.IR P ]
.br
.B runner status
.RI [ \-\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B runner selftest
.RI [ host ]
.br
.B runner version
.br
.B runner help
.SH DESCRIPTION
A clean-room reimplementation of the GitHub Actions runner wire protocol in
C99, for IRIX 6.5.22 and later. The official runner is .NET and cannot run
there.
.PP
The runtime is split client/server, and one binary is both halves. The server
holds the registration and long-polls GitHub for work. The client is the job
runtime: it takes one job as a message file, runs the steps and reports.
.PP
.B run
is both halves in one process and is what an SGI uses.
.B serve
is the server alone, for a pool of registered identities on a Linux host, and
hands each job it acquires to a container.
.B execjob
is the client alone, needs no registration, and reads the job message from a
file.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS configure
Registers with GitHub and writes the runner state. Run once. Generates a
2048\-bit RSA key and sends the public half; the registration token is not
needed again, because every identity authenticates with that key from then on.
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
.I https://github.com/ORG
or
.IR https://github.com/ORG/REPO .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
A registration token, from the repository or organisation Settings page, or
from
.IR /repos/OWNER/REPO/actions/runners/registration-token .
They expire in one hour. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Runner name. Defaults to the hostname, or
.I irix\-runner
when
.BR gethostname (3)
fails. Excluded by
.BR \-\-count .
.TP
.BI \-\-runnergroup " NAME"
Runner group, default
.IR Default .
See
.B NOTES
below: a wrong group is silent.
.TP
.BI \-\-labels " A,B,C"
Extra labels beyond the
.IR irix ", " mips " and " mips\-n32
every runner carries. At most 32 labels in total.
.TP
.BI \-\-work " DIR"
Work folder, default
.IR _work .
Excluded by
.BR \-\-count ,
which gives every identity its own.
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Take over an existing runner of this name. Without it, an existing
.I .runner
in the target directory is refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
Register
.I N
identities rather than one, 1 to 64. Creates
.IR P\-0 " through " P\-(N\-1)
under the current directory, each named after its own directory, and adds an
.I emulated
label. Requires
.BR \-\-name\-prefix ,
and excludes
.BR \-\-name " and " \-\-work .
.TP
.BI \-\-name\-prefix " P"
The prefix for
.BR \-\-count .
Names both the directory and the runner. At most 112 bytes.
.SS run
Listens for jobs and executes them in this process. This is what makes the
runner show Online. Runs on IRIX and on Linux.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Runner directory, default the current one.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-\-trace
Protocol logging, increasing.
.SS serve
One listener per identity, each job in its own container. Linux only; on IRIX
it prints a message and returns 2.
.PP
Forks one child per identity, all before any network use, because the HTTP
client caches one keep\-alive TLS connection per host and sharing it across
children corrupts the stream. Every directory is checked before any fork, so a
missing one aborts the whole command.
.PP
.BR SIGTERM " or " SIGINT
is forwarded to every child exactly once, and the parent then waits for all of
them, so no identity is left holding a pool session. A
.B serve
that starts after an unclean exit reaps the containers its predecessor left
behind, identified by a
.I sgug.runner.supervisor
label naming a pid that no longer exists.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
Serve
.I N
identities, 1 to 64. Goes with
.BR \-\-name\-prefix .
.TP
.BI \-\-name\-prefix " P"
Directories
.IR P\-0 ", " P\-1 ", ..."
.TP
.BI \-\-image " NAME"
Worker image, default
.IR irix\-worker:latest .
An image the daemon does not have is pulled once and the create retried.
.TP
.BI \-\-job\-timeout " SECS"
Wall clock per job, 1 to 86400, default 14400. Measured with
.B CLOCK_MONOTONIC
from the moment the container starts. On expiry the container is killed and the
job is reported failed from the host. Host\-side only: it is never propagated
into the container.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-\-trace
Protocol logging, increasing.
.SS execjob
Runs one job from a message file and reports it. Needs no configuration,
because the message carries the credentials it reports with. This is what runs
inside the worker container.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " FILE"
The job message as received. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
The runner name the job sees. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-work " DIR"
Work folder. Must be absolute, and under 128 bytes. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-cancel\-file " PATH"
Abort when this file's mtime changes. The file must already exist. Polled every
5 seconds by a
.B SIGALRM
handler.
.SS remove
Deregisters and deletes the local configuration. Takes the same
.BR \-\-count " and " \-\-name\-prefix
as
.BR configure ,
and a fresh
.BR \-\-token .
Unlike
.BR configure ,
it continues past a failure and returns 1 at the end, so one unreachable
identity does not strand the rest.
.SS status
Prints the configured runner: name, URL, group and pool id, agent id, tenant,
whether the v2 broker flow is in use, the JWT signing algorithm and the work
folder. Takes
.BI \-\-dir " DIR" .
Returns 1 when nothing is configured there.
.SS selftest
Opens an HTTPS connection to
.I host
(default
.IR api.github.com )
and reports the status, the server header, the body size, the clock skew
against the server's
.B Date
header, whether the JSON parses, and whether a second request reuses the
connection.
.PP
Run it before anything else on an SGI: a wrong clock and an expired CA bundle
are the two things that break a fresh install, and both produce confusing
errors later. It checks nothing about Docker, so on a Linux host
.B selftest OK
says nothing about whether
.B serve
will work.
.SS version
Prints this runner's version and the protocol version it reports to the
service. Also
.BR \-\-version " and " \-V .
.SS help
Prints the usage summary. Also
.BR \-\-help " and " \-h .
.SH LABELS
Every runner carries
.IR irix ", " mips " and " mips\-n32 ,
plus the system labels
.IR self\-hosted ", " Linux " and " X64 .
The last two are untrue and deliberate: GitHub's system label vocabulary has no
IRIX or MIPS value, and a runner describing itself accurately would match no
.IR runs\-on .
.PP
.B configure \-\-count
adds
.IR emulated ,
so
.I runs\-on: [self\-hosted, irix, emulated]
pins a job to a container pool.
.I runs\-on
is an AND over labels with no negation, so nothing excludes that pool; keeping
work on real hardware needs a label of its own from
.BR \-\-labels .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .runner
Agent id, name, pool and server URLs. Mode 0644.
.TP
.I .credentials
OAuth client id and token endpoint. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I .rsakey
The private key, PKCS#1 PEM. Mode 0600. A warning is printed if the mode is
anything else.
.TP
.I cert.pem
Trust roots. Adopted automatically when it sits beside the binary.
.PP
Under
.B \-\-count
there is one set of the first three per identity directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SGUG_RUNNER_OS
The OS the runner claims. Default
.IR Linux ,
see
.BR LABELS .
Reaches the acquirejob request, the message poll query and the
.B RUNNER_OS
variable given to steps.
.TP
.B SSL_CERT_FILE
Trust roots. Set automatically from a
.I cert.pem
beside the binary when unset. SGUG\-RSE's own bundle at
.I /usr/sgug/etc/pki/tls/cert.pem
is used when neither is present.
.TP
.B DOCKER_HOST
Overrides
.IR /var/run/docker.sock .
Only a
.I unix://
path is accepted; any other form is an error rather than a silent fallback.
.B serve
only.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Where
.B serve
creates each job's staging directory, mode 0700. Defaults to
.IR /tmp .
.TP
.B SGUG_DUMP_MESSAGES
Prints every message body received. Job messages carry access tokens and every
secret the workflow references, so this belongs in a debugging session and
nowhere else.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command ran and failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, an unknown command, or
.B serve
on IRIX.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register one runner against a repository and start it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
runner configure \-\-url https://github.com/OWNER/REPO \-\-token TOK
runner run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Register four identities against an organisation, in a group that has access to
the repositories whose workflows are queued, and serve them:
.PP
.RS
.nf
runner configure \-\-url https://github.com/ORG \-\-token TOK \\
    \-\-count 4 \-\-name\-prefix irix \-\-runnergroup IRIX
runner serve \-\-count 4 \-\-name\-prefix irix \\
    \-\-image ghcr.io/sgidevnet/irix\-worker:0.4.3\-indy
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
A wrong
.B \-\-runnergroup
is quiet. The runner registers, shows Online, and is never dispatched to,
because the group it landed in has no access to the repository whose workflow
is queued. The group's repository access is under the organisation's Actions
settings.
.PP
Nothing renews a job lock. A job that is acquired and never completed leaves
that identity online at
.I currentParallelism 1
and never dispatched to again.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR gh (1)
.PP
.I https://github.com/sgidevnet/irix\-actions\-runner
.PP
.I docs/protocol.md
in the source tree records where github.com diverges from its own published
documentation.
